// CROWN A5 (LENS §2.4, the arm-world rule): resuming inside an arm of h
// continues the REMAINDER under h, so a handler's own declared negation
// binds what the remainder performs minus what h absorbs. h declares !F
// and is installed over a body whose remainder performs F after op: the
// arm's resume continues into F, so the install REFUSES (E_EffectMismatch
// naming h). RED-first on boot 39b00d84: accepted, no diagnostic — the
// handler's negation bound only the arms' own performs.
effect E { op() -> Int }
effect F { fop() -> Int }
handler h with !F { op() => resume(1) }
handler hf { fop() => resume(2) }
fn work() = op() + fop()
fn main() = ((work()) ~> h) ~> hf
